          "items": [
            {
              "key": "nEn",
              "role": "markdown",
              "content": [
                {
                  "code": "nl",
                  "parts": [
                    {
                      "str": "If you agree, UKHSA will contact you by email with a link to a partner website (Take a Test UK) to provide additional information. Your information will be handled securely by Take a Test UK and limited information will be shared with UKHSA to enable us to identify your sample and test results. \n\n \n\nPlease note that by agreeing to participate in self-swabbing, you understand that: \n\n* Your test results will be held securely by UKHSA and can be linked back to your survey data \n* You will receive certain test results (such as flu and COVID-19) but this test is not intended as a clinical diagnosis or to inform your treatment. If you need urgent results for your individual care, you should not use this service. \n* To help us understand risk factors and outcomes of respiratory viruses, your test results will be linked to securely held health data at UKHSA, such as previous immunisations and administrative health records    \n* These test results will only be sent to you and not to your GP \n* You can find full details about how your data will be used, stored, and protected - including the process of withdrawing from the study - in our [Privacy Notice](https://flusurvey.net/legal/privacy-postal-swabbing)"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
